module Core

### The protocol for a value that can be STORED at an implicit-copy site.
### `Storable` gates the `=` operator and every position that implicitly copies a value:
### `var x = a`, passing as a non-`steal` argument, returning a non-`T` value, and `with`
### lens-copy. Auto-derived for any type whose `@llvm` layout contains no `ptr` (and for
### `@llvm("void")`). Types with managed-pointer payloads (`Retained[T]`, `Text`, …) opt in by
### writing `obeys Storable` and a `store` body that spells out each field's verb (a refcount
### bump / COW share), centralising the cost in one visible place. `Copyable obeys Storable`:
### a deep-`copy`-able value is always `store`-able, and a `store`-able value is always assignable.
### `needs Storable everywhere` auto-confers Storable on any member-bearing type all of whose members
### are themselves Storable — the structural gate that drives the auto-derived `store`.
protocol Storable
needs Storable everywhere
  ### Produces the value to bind at the store/assignment destination. For auto-derived types this
  ### is a bitwise duplicate; for opt-in managed types it is the cheap COW share (e.g. a refcount
  ### bump). The heavier deep, independent duplicate is `Copyable.copy`.
  ### :returns: The value to store into the destination slot.
  @[readonly, inline]
  routine Me.store() -> Me
